    q: `A 71-year-old male with multiple comorbidities (CAD, diabetes, COPD on home oxygen, osteoporosis, history of DVT 2 years ago now on warfarin, mild cognitive impairment) is admitted for emergency (not elective) spinal fusion for cord compression. Time is limited—surgery is in 2 hours. Extensive pre-op assessment is not possible. The pre-op nurse must PRIORITIZE which critical assessments and interventions? (SELECT ALL THAT APPLY)`,
