    a: "TURP syndrome from hypervolemia and hyponatremia due to absorption of large volume of hypotonic irrigation fluid; glycine absorbed systemically causes additional neurologic effects; presents with hypertension (early), bradycardia (increased ICP), confusion (hyponatremia + hyperammonemia from glycine); treatment: fluid restriction, hypertonic saline, diuretics, monitor for seizures/cerebral edema",
