    a: "Prior unexplained intra-operative fever is a RED FLAG for possible MH; even if MH wasn't recognized then, patient should now have MH-safe anesthesia (non-triggering agents); take DETAILED history of ALL prior anesthetics, any intra-operative fever or complications; if history suggests possible MH, use non-triggering anesthesia and have dantrolene available",
