    rationale: `This SATA tests comprehensive post-operative MH management and anticipatory problem prevention. Analysis: (1) STATEMENT A (Continue dantrolene post-op): CORRECT—Standard protocol after MH crisis is dantrolene 1 mg/kg IV q4-6h for 24-48 hours. Recrudescence (late MH recurrence) can occur in ~3% of cases. Must prevent it. (2) STATEMENT B (Laboratory monitoring): CORRECT—Essential labs: CPK (extent of rhabdomyolysis), K+ (myoglobin release causes hyperkalemia), urinalysis (detect myoglobinuria), renal function (BUN, Creatinine). AKI is a major post-MH complication. (3) STATEMENT C (Never general anesthesia again): INCORRECT/OVERSTATED—Patient can undergo general anesthesia again IF using MH-SAFE anesthesia (non-triggering agents). Absolute exclusion from GA is too restrictive. With proper precautions, surgery is possible. (4) STATEMENT D (Aggressive hydration, alkaline urine): CORRECT—Critical management to prevent rhabdomyolysis-induced AKI. IV fluids to maintain UOP >1-2 mL/kg/hr. Sodium bicarbonate to alkalinize urine (pH >6.5). In alkaline urine, myoglobin stays soluble and won't precipitate in tubules. (5) STATEMENT E (Discharge today): INCORRECT—Patient must remain in ICU/hospital for close monitoring. At minimum 24-48 hours of observation. CPK may continue rising. Creatinine may worsen. Recrudescence can occur. Labs checked frequently (not just daily—more like q4-6h initially). (6) STATEMENT F (Genetic counseling, family screening): CORRECT—MH is autosomal dominant. Family members (siblings, children) have 50% risk. Genetic testing (RYR1, CACNA1S mutations) should be offered. Family members should receive education about MH-safe anesthesia for their future surgeries. (7) KEY INSIGHT: MH crisis doesn't end at extubation. Post-op management is complex and extended. Why he manifested MH despite non-triggering drugs: Unknown (incomplete penetrance, genetic factors, possible stress-induced late MH). But fact that he manifested confirms he IS susceptible and MUST be managed as such forever. (8) CORRECT ANSWERS: A, B, D, F. These address post-op dantrolene continuation, comprehensive lab monitoring, AKI prevention, and family genetic counseling. Statements C and E are incorrect or overstated.`,
